1. Scope

   This license covers the Bridger source code, headers, build files, tools, scripts,
   documentation and artwork in this repository (the "Software"), and the binaries built
   from them.

2. What you may do

   You may read the Software, and you may clone, build and run it on your own machine for
   your own use, subject to section 4.

3. Mods

   You may write, build and distribute mods for Bridger, in source or binary form, free
   of charge or for money, under any terms you choose, provided that the mod:

   a. is your own work, or work you are licensed to distribute;
   b. uses the Software only through its public interface, meaning the headers under
      include/bridger, the Lua API, and the manifest and configuration formats;
   c. does not include, bundle or redistribute the Software itself, in whole or in part,
      and directs its users to obtain Bridger from the copyright holder; and
   d. does not include or redistribute any file from Death Stranding or anything derived
      from one.

   Nothing in this section makes your mod part of the Software, and nothing in it grants
   you any rights in the Software beyond what section 2 already does.

4. A copy of the game you own

   Bridger works by modifying a running copy of Death Stranding. You may use the
   Software only with a copy of Death Stranding that you own or are licensed to use,
   obtained through a legitimate channel. Using the Software with a pirated, cracked or
   otherwise unauthorised copy of the game is outside this license, and no right granted
   here applies to that use.

   Your agreement with the game's publisher and with the platform it runs on is between
   you and them. This license grants nothing with respect to the game, and the copyright
   holder makes no claim that using the Software is permitted under that agreement. That
   judgement, and its consequences, are yours.

   The Software checks this when it starts. It confirms that the game's own steam_api64.dll
   carries Valve's signature, then asks the Steam client whether the signed-in account
   holds a licence for Death Stranding. When either answer is no, the Software loads
   nothing: no mods, no scripts, no overlay. Removing, disabling or working around that
   check is a breach of this license.

5. What you may not do without written permission from the copyright holder

   a. Copy, publish or redistribute the Software or any part of it, in source or binary
      form, modified or unmodified.
   b. Distribute software that includes or is derived from the Software, other than a
      mod that meets section 3.
   c. Sell, sublicense, rent or otherwise make the Software available to third parties.
   d. Remove or alter this notice or any copyright, authorship or attribution notice in
      the Software.

   Permission requests may be sent to the copyright holder. A permission granted in
   writing applies only to what it names.

6. What this license does not cover

   a. Third-party components fetched or bundled by the build keep their own licenses and
      their own copyright holders. As of this writing these are MinHook (BSD-2-Clause,
      Tsuda Kageyu), nlohmann/json (MIT, Niels Lohmann) and Lua (MIT, Lua.org, PUC-Rio).
      Their notices apply to the built binaries.
   b. Death Stranding, the Decima engine and everything derived from them belong to their
      owners. This repository ships no game files. Anything the tools generate from your
      own copy of the game (type databases, engine headers, shader dumps, captures) stays
      on your machine and is not licensed by this document.

